# Make `AGENTS.md` default to SHAR mod authoring and validate C++ with Clang

Split agent guidance between repository engineering and a default mod-authoring
personality. A user who downloads the repository and opens it in a coding agent
should be guided toward making or repairing a SHAR mod unless they explicitly
request repository-development work.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Make the mod-authoring reading path the default user-facing agent posture
  while preserving a clearly separated repository-engineering path.
- [ ] Include prompt examples for repairing incomplete LMLM conversions,
  creating a boss fight after a mission, and changing world/mission coordinates.
- [ ] Teach agents to request missing lawful assets and ask how the mod should
  behave instead of inventing unavailable legacy behavior.
- [ ] Do not add an agent-only guardrail that pretends a local mod is impossible
  to inspect; actual converter policy is enforced by converter code/config.
- [ ] Make C++ the supported native mod-code language and run the same strict
  Clang-family validation contract used by SHAR before recommending release.
- [ ] Allow manual mod authorship "for some reason"; source can be written by
  hand, but published validation should clearly report lint/compiler failures.
- [ ] Update README examples when the final agent workflow changes.

## Dependencies

Depends on final user-facing mod skills and the SHAR mod package contract.

